Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||12-07-2000||06:11 PM||||Hello All, <BR> I was trying to fix my washer pump. I tested it for power, nada! I followed the hot pink power wire back into the firewall looking for a snag, or a break in the line. I couldn't follow it under the steering column, so I am left with the guesstimation, (nice word) of a problem with the turn signal stalk. Any info would be greatly appreciated. If it is the Stalk, how do you remove with out breaking. Thanks, in advance<BR>Chris <BR><P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||12-07-2000||08:03 PM||||The only wiring in the stalk itself is for cruise if you have it. The wiper stuff is in the column||||reg||1
Z||000002||Johnson's85SE||12-08-2000||02:28 PM||||So what exactly is not delivering power? Is there a switch in the column? Where is the Swith? To me it seems like the swith is just not opening to send power to the unit. <BR>Cheers!<BR>Chris<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||12-08-2000||05:31 PM||||From what I was told, there is a switch in the colomn at the end of the turn signal stalk.  There are tabs (2?)on the stalk that operate the switch or at least that's where the linkage is that operates it.  Now I haven't dug into mine to see what the heck he's talking about, but at least I got the idea I don't have to change the stalk that has the cruise controll in it.  He did mention the tabs may have been broken off the stalk, but I think I can see them without having the colomn apart yet.  That's as far as I've gotten on the subject.  I think I'm going to get one of those tools to take apart the colomn first.  It's a pain without it.  good luck. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
